Embedded players
The Suno and Spotify chips embed players from suno.com and open.spotify.com.
Their content and terms belong to those services.

Sample media (media/, source-materials/)
The sample set exists so the board has something to show. It is for demo and
trial use only, not commercial use, and it is not part of the MIT grant. Do not
re-publish, sell or use it in a product. If you are a rights holder and want
something removed, open an issue and it will be taken down.
- media/music: instrumental sample tracks generated by the author with Google's Lyria
  RealTime model through the Gemini API (prompts in tools/sample-audio-prompts.md).
  Google marks Lyria output with an inaudible SynthID watermark. The tracks are
  not recordings of existing songs. Check Google's terms before commercial reuse.
  The sample lyrics (tools/sample-lyrics.md) are original text written for this
  repository. Cues and lead sheets are placeholders, not transcriptions of the audio.
- media/loops, source-materials/thumbnails: short video loops generated by the
  author locally with ComfyUI-based models (the moody loops with MiniMax H3
  text-to-video), made seamless by playing forward then backward, silent and
  re-encoded for the web. Check the model terms before commercial reuse.
- media/3d: instrument models generated from reference images with TRELLIS.2
  and normalised in Blender. Reference images are not included.
- media/charts: form charts drawn by tools/make-demo-data.py from the sample
  audio. Lyrics for the first sample song are the author's.

The black-box venue in the 3D view is a sample room. Its dimensions follow a
public venue specification sheet; no venue branding is included.
